                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2024-04-26T17:57:13Z'>
              <span itemprop='position'>13</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop='text'>
              <p>Roblox historically is awful at keeping to their promises, and especially bad at fully developing new features before forgetting they exist outright and breaking them due to their awful quality control, ie users wishing to use Vulkan lighting which dramatically improves performance over DX11 for high-end systems no longer auto-switches, when it used to many years ago, resulting in awful performance on high-end machines.</p>
<p>WHY has future lighting still not fixed its shadow overlap bug? <s>Why have bugs that stem from floating-point inaccuracy not being addressed not been fixed or patched in the ways that are trivial across all other open-world engines and games in the entire industry? Why do we not have better control over outright making our own physics and lighting engines to actively replace the existing ones?</s></p>
            </div>

            <div itemprop="interactionStatistic" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/InteractionCounter">
              <meta itemprop="interactionType" content="http://schema.org/LikeAction"/>
              <meta itemprop="userInteractionCount" content="18" />
              <span class='post-likes'>18 Likes</span>
            </div>

          </div>
          <div id='post_14' itemprop='comment' itemscope itemtype='http://schema.org/Comment' class='topic-body crawler-post'>
            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>
              <span class="creator" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person">
                <a itemprop="url" rel='nofollow' href='https://devforum.roblox.com/u/SilentFish20'><span itemprop='name'>SilentFish20</span></a>
                (rolbloxbro73465)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop='datePublished' datetime='2024-04-26T17:56:19Z' class='post-time'>
                    April 26, 2024,  5:56pm
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2024-04-26T17:56:19Z'>
              <span itemprop='position'>14</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop='text'>
              <p>It’s a mix of priority and mobile. Mobile ultimatley stops roblox achieving things I’m sure the devs would love to do. But not just that. Is fixing a future lighting bug going to make them money? No. So it isn’t on the to-do list.</p>
            </div>

            <div itemprop="interactionStatistic" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/InteractionCounter">
              <meta itemprop="interactionType" content="http://schema.org/LikeAction"/>
              <meta itemprop="userInteractionCount" content="14" />
              <span class='post-likes'>14 Likes</span>
            </div>

          </div>
          <div id='post_15' itemprop='comment' itemscope itemtype='http://schema.org/Comment' class='topic-body crawler-post'>
            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>
              <span class="creator" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person">
                <a itemprop="url" rel='nofollow' href='https://devforum.roblox.com/u/BritishTrainspotting'><span itemprop='name'>BritishTrainspotting</span></a>
                (BritishTrainspotter)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop='datePublished' datetime='2024-04-26T17:57:45Z' class='post-time'>
                    April 26, 2024,  5:57pm
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2024-04-26T18:00:29Z'>
              <span itemprop='position'>15</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop='text'>
              <p>Just because something doesn’t directly make a profit doesn’t mean it has no effect, anyone who has a basic understanding of business knows that, and Roblox clearly aren’t very good at such.</p>
<p><em><strong>Better developer satisfaction and tools means more productivity, more productivity means more polished game updates and more frequent game updates, such as new gamepasses or developer products, new updates and more refined updates means more user satisfaction, and more user satisfaction means the user is more likely to buy gamepasses or developer products, thus more likely to buy Robux, which earns Roblox money.</strong></em> Done, simple.</p>
<p>Developers won’t be motivated by the development process being difficult or actively made worse.<br>
Player’s won’t buy items for a game that they dislike.<br>
Players WILL buy items for a game they enjoy, and will play a game for longer if they enjoy it.</p>
            </div>

            <div itemprop="interactionStatistic" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/InteractionCounter">
              <meta itemprop="interactionType" content="http://schema.org/LikeAction"/>
              <meta itemprop="userInteractionCount" content="13" />
              <span class='post-likes'>13 Likes</span>
            </div>

          </div>
          <div id='post_16' itemprop='comment' itemscope itemtype='http://schema.org/Comment' class='topic-body crawler-post'>
            <div class='crawler-post-meta'>
              <span class="creator" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person">
                <a itemprop="url" rel='nofollow' href='https://devforum.roblox.com/u/abidbmt'><span itemprop='name'>abidbmt</span></a>
                (abid)
              </span>



              <span class="crawler-post-infos">
                  <time itemprop='datePublished' datetime='2024-04-26T18:00:09Z' class='post-time'>
                    April 26, 2024,  6:00pm
                  </time>
                  <meta itemprop='dateModified' content='2024-04-27T17:23:50Z'>
              <span itemprop='position'>16</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class='post' itemprop='text'>
              <p>In my opinion, Roblox doesn’t focus enough on their existing engine features and performance; e.g., R6 really deserves an upgrade with its extremely high popularity and usage among popular Roblox games. Roblox has such great potential as an engine, but that is wasted on features that either no one asked for (therefore creating unneeded issues and work) or should have been added later after more important features and improvements were made.</p>
            </div>

